        # (re-entrant: nested callptr → distinct slots), so it survives
        # ECALLPOPS — which on Win64 sub's rsp for the 32 B shadow home and
        # would bury a stack-pushed callee. Then push args, marshal, and call
        # through the slot via ECALLIND (call [rbp-disp] / ldr x6;blr x6).
        # Result (the callee's return) lands in rax/x0 like any call.
        # The spill is a frame local, so callptr needs a function frame —
        # top-level vars are globals (no rbp frame). Fail loud, not crash.
