            # below would produce an `0F 05` syscall that faults
            # at runtime on Windows with STATUS_ILLEGAL_INSTRUCTION
            # (0xC000001D). Routed numbers (v5.11.22, +v6.0.51, +v6.0.54):
            # 0=read, 1=write, 2=open, 3=close, 8=lseek, 9=mmap,
            # 60=exit, 83=mkdir, 87=unlink, 228=clock_gettime, and
            # 0xF001-0xF005 = Win32 process creation (Wait/GetExit/
